  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Evidence-Based Protection Assistance for Populations Affected by Natural Hazards in Burundi</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Burundi continues to be affected by climate hazards which exacerbate existing socioeconomic vulnerabilities and heighten humanitarian needs. It is also located in an earthquake-prone geographic zone of the African Great Lakes, increasing exposure to catastrophic events. Approximately ninety per cent of internal displacement in Burundi of late is triggered by climate hazards causing the loss of lives and the destruction of croplands, homes and public infrastructure. 
 
The International Organization for Migration (IOM) is providing protection assistance to save lives and respond to the urgent needs of 5,000 individuals affected by natural hazards in Makamba and Ruyigi provinces. This project supports the Government of Burundi&#x2019;s response to internal displacement through rapid and regular data collection, analysis and monitoring to provide appropriate lifesaving assistance to vulnerable groups and evidence-based protection assistance.</narrative>
  </description>
